            "sort": 3,
            "name": "Body 1",
            "value": "<p>Looking at Denmark and Sweden, both countries displayed a similar pattern, with the 36-40 hour bracket accounting for approximately 70% and 80% of workers, respectively. In Denmark, the second most common category was 31-35 hours at 22%, while the remaining brackets each recorded roughly 10%. Sweden showed a wider distribution, with 36% of employees working 31-35 hours and 29% in the 41-45 hour range.</p>",
